# CARE Frontend

You are an expert in TypeScript, React, Shadcn UI, Tailwind, and CARE frontend development.

CARE is a Digital Public Good and Hospital Management Information System (HMIS) that enables TeleICU operations and decentralized administration of healthcare capacity across healthcare facilities.

## Key Principles

- Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)

## Naming Conventions

- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., patient-management/, facility-overview/)
- Favor named exports for components
- Use PascalCase for components (PatientOverview, FacilityList)
- Use camelCase for functions and variables (fetchData, isLoading)

## TypeScript Usage

- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types for data structures
- Avoid enums; use maps instead (except for medical constants like BloodGroupChoices)
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- Strict typing for all data and API interfaces

## Syntax and Formatting

- Use the "function" keyword for pure functions
- Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals; use concise syntax for simple statements
- Use declarative JSX
- Handle data with proper null checks and error boundaries

## UI and Styling

- Use Shadcn UI, Radix, and Tailwind for components and styling
- Use CAREUI for custom components (Calendar, forms)
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind CSS; use a mobile-first approach

## Data & API Guidelines

- CARE uses TanStack Query for data fetching with query and mutate utilities (src/Utils/request/README.md)
- APIs are defined in \*.Api.ts files under src/types/ directories
- Use zod validation for all data inputs
- Handle data with appropriate security measures

## Routing & Navigation

- Use raviger for routing
- Organize routes by domains (Patient/, Facility/, etc.)
- Implement proper navigation history

## Internationalization

- Add and reuse proper translations in en.json
- Use consistent term translations across components
- Support date/time formatting

## Standards

- WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility compliance
- Proper error boundaries for critical data

## Testing Guidelines

For Playwright testing guidelines, refer to tests/README.md for testing patterns.

## Reference

See .github/copilot-instructions.md and .cursor/rules/\*.mdc for comprehensive guidance.
